    "hairscripts_faq_split_MWpNL3": {
      "type": "hairscripts-faq-split",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_aYjpAY": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Will this work on my hair type or texture?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. HairScripts™ works on all hair types, textures, and patterns — straight, wavy, curly, coily, fine, or thick. The science behind hair growth is the same for everyone. Your follicles need the same nutrients, the same circulation, the same hormonal balance, and the same protection from oxidative stress regardless of what your strands look like above the scalp.</p><p>This formula was built to support the root cause of thinning, not the strand itself. That means it works underneath your texture — supporting follicle health from the inside out.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_hBGTxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm on Ozempic, Wegovy, or another GLP-1 medication. Will this work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — and you may actually need this more than most. GLP-1 medications significantly reduce appetite, which often means a significant drop in protein, iron, zinc, and Vitamin D intake. Combined with the metabolic stress of rapid weight loss, this triggers a delayed shedding pattern that shows up 2–4 months in.</p><p>HairScripts™ was formulated to address exactly this kind of nutritional gap. Bioavailable iron, zinc, Vitamin D, collagen, and pea protein directly replace what GLP-1 users tend to lose. Ashwagandha supports the cortisol response to major metabolic shifts.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_iNbfbe": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm postpartum or breastfeeding — can I take this?",
            "answer": "<p>Postpartum yes, breastfeeding requires a conversation with your provider. The formula was designed with postpartum recovery in mind — it addresses the iron depletion, hormonal crash, and stress-related shedding that typically appear 3–6 months after delivery.</p><p>If you're currently breastfeeding, please review the ingredients with your healthcare provider before starting. While the ingredients are generally well-tolerated, your individual situation should be evaluated by someone who knows your medical history.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_B3Vw9i": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I'm in perimenopause or menopause. Will this work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>This is one of the patterns the formula was specifically built around. As estrogen declines, your follicles become more sensitive to androgen activity. At the same time, cortisol regulation shifts, antioxidant defense drops, and the protective hormonal environment that kept your follicles in the growth phase starts to disappear.</p><p>HairScripts™ supports healthy DHT activity, cortisol balance, scalp circulation, and the antioxidant layer your body loses access to during this transition. All in one daily formula.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Hchjtn": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Will this work if I have PCOS/PMOS, insulin resistance, or thyroid issues?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes for most situations. PCOS/PMOS and insulin resistance raise androgen activity at the follicle, and thyroid dysfunction slows follicle cell division — these root causes need to be addressed at the source, not at the strand. HairScripts™ supports insulin sensitivity, healthy DHT activity, and the selenium and zinc pathways that support thyroid-related follicle function.</p><p>HairScripts™ contains Ashwagandha, which has clinical research supporting subclinical and underactive thyroid function (hypothyroidism, Hashimoto's). However, women with hyperthyroidism or Graves' disease should speak with their provider before starting — Ashwagandha can increase thyroid hormone production, which is helpful when your thyroid is underactive and a concern when it's overactive. The same conversation applies if you're currently on thyroid replacement medication like levothyroxine.</p><p>Please continue any prescribed medications — HairScripts™ is designed to work alongside them, not replace them.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6KNWc7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Can I take this with other supplements or prescription medications?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is generally compatible with most supplements and medications. However, since the formula contains iron, zinc, and clinically-active ingredients like Saw Palmetto and Ashwagandha, please review the ingredient list with your healthcare provider if you are on prescription medications — especially blood thinners, hormone therapies, thyroid medications, sedatives, immunosuppressants, or antidepressants.</p><p>If you're already taking a separate iron or multivitamin, you may not need it anymore once you start HairScripts™. Check with your provider to avoid stacking.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_T3TfGm": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "I've tried everything — nothing has worked. Why would this be different?",
            "answer": "<p>Because most of what you tried was built around one pathway. Biotin focuses on a single vitamin. Most hair growth supplements on the market focus on one or two pathways at most. Meanwhile your hair loss is probably being driven by 3–5 root causes simultaneously — stress, hormones, nutrient depletion, inflammation, and circulation.</p><p>HairScripts™ was built differently. It addresses all 9 root causes of hormonal hair loss in one formula — so you're covered at every level, even if you haven't identified the specific trigger yet. The formula didn't fail you before. The formulas you tried were built for one problem and you have nine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_f9Gmmf": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Can men use this too?",
            "answer": "<p>The formula was specifically developed for women navigating hormonal hair loss — the patterns that show up during postpartum, perimenopause, stress, and metabolic shifts. While men can technically take it, the dosing and ingredient profile were calibrated around female hormonal biology.</p><p>For men experiencing hair loss, the underlying drivers are typically different and may require a different formulation strategy. We don't currently have a men's formula, but it may be on the horizon.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_VNqzEc": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_1",
            "question": "Is this for all hair types and textures?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes — HairScripts works on all hair types, textures, and patterns. Hair biology is universal. If your follicles are weakened, this formula supports regrowth at the root level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BCBBnr": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "What makes HairScripts™ different from other hair growth supplements?",
            "answer": "<p>Three things. First, HairScripts™ addresses all 9 root causes of hormonal hair loss simultaneously — not one pathway at a time. Most supplements on the market focus on a single ingredient or one or two pathways. That's why they fail for most women whose hair loss is being driven by 3–5 root causes at once.</p><p>Second, every ingredient is clinically dosed at levels research actually supports — not micro-dosed for marketing appeal. Many supplements list impressive-sounding ingredients in doses too small to do anything.</p><p>Third, this formula was developed by a pharmaceutical industry expert who personally lost nearly 60% of her hair and had the clinical training to understand exactly why. That combination — multi-pathway formulation, clinical dosing, and pharmaceutical-grade development — is the entire difference.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_VkfP8N": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Is this just another biotin pill?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Biotin alone fails for most women because hair growth requires far more than one vitamin. Your follicles rely on iron, zinc, Vitamin D, selenium, copper, and absorption cofactors working together — alongside hormonal balance, cortisol regulation, scalp circulation, and antioxidant defense.</p><p>HairScripts™ was built as a coordinated system, not a single-ingredient shortcut. Biotin alone is like trying to build a house with only one tool.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Qi3MJ7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "I've read concerns about Ashwagandha. Is it safe in this formula?",
            "answer": "<p>Ashwagandha is one of the most clinically studied adaptogens in modern science — with thousands of years of traditional use and dozens of peer-reviewed studies on cortisol reduction, stress-related shedding, and follicle recovery. The research is robust and the safety profile is well-documented.</p><p>That said, Ashwagandha is not the right fit for everyone. Women with hyperthyroidism or Graves' disease should avoid it. Women on thyroid replacement medication should speak with their provider first. Women who are pregnant should also consult their healthcare provider before starting.</p><p>If you have any underlying condition or you're on prescription medications, please review the full ingredient list with your healthcare provider before starting. That goes for every supplement, not just this one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_3CtYRi": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Why does HairScripts™ require 4 capsules per day?",
            "answer": "<p>Because clinical dosing requires it. To deliver every ingredient at the levels research actually supports, 4 capsules is what fits the volume.</p><p>Single-capsule formulas exist, but they exist by under-dosing every ingredient. We chose to dose at clinical levels instead. Take all 4 daily, with or without food, for best results.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_cpeKzP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": " Is this drug-free? Does it contain minoxidil?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, it's drug-free. No, it does not contain minoxidil — or any prescription pharmaceutical. HairScripts™ is a science-backed dietary supplement formulated with clinically-studied vitamins, minerals, botanical extracts, and amino acids.</p><p>Minoxidil works for some women, but it requires lifelong topical application, can cause rebound shedding when stopped, and only addresses one pathway. HairScripts™ is the alternative — a multi-pathway system that supports your follicles from the inside without prescription side effects.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nQVh7C": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Is HairScripts™ third-party tested?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. HairScripts™ is manufactured in a GMP-certified facility and undergoes third-party testing for purity, potency, and contaminant screening. The formula was reviewed and approved by a licensed healthcare provider before launch.</p><p>You deserve to know exactly what's going into your body — and that the dose on the label matches what's actually in the capsule. We take that responsibility seriously.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_86rwCb": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "Where is HairScripts™ manufactured?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is manufactured in the United States in a GMP-certified facility. Every batch is tested for purity, potency, and contaminants before shipping.</p><p>Manufacturing transparency matters in the supplement industry — and we believe you should be able to trust that what's on the label is what's in the bottle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_9ibBAW": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_2",
            "question": "What's in HairScripts™? Is the formula transparent?",
            "answer": "<p>Every ingredient is listed on the label with its specific clinical dose. No proprietary blends. No hidden actives. No marketing-only ingredients.</p><p>For the full formula, check out the supplement facts on the product page.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_R4WqzN": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "How soon will I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>Most women notice less shedding within 4–8 weeks, and visible density improvements between 90 days and 6 months. Hair grows in months, not days — that's not a marketing limitation, that's how the growth cycle actually works. It takes at least 90 days to biohack your body from a cellular level.</p><p>Consistency is the variable that determines your timeline. Take 4 capsules daily without skipping. Most women who quit at week 6 quit right before the results would have started showing up. Don't be one of them.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_iKeBzF": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "I've heard supplements can cause more shedding before improvement. Is that true with HairScripts™?",
            "answer": "<p>This is a common concern, and it deserves an honest answer. HairScripts™ is a multi-pathway nutritional formula — not a vascular stimulant — so it does not work the way topical treatments like minoxidil do. Most women using HairScripts™ do not experience increased shedding when starting the formula.</p><p>That said, hair growth is a complex biological process, and individual responses vary based on your underlying root cause, hormonal status, stress levels, and consistency. If you notice changes in your shedding pattern, give the formula at least 90 days — that's the minimum timeline for the growth cycle to reflect what's happening internally.</p><p>If you have concerns about your specific situation, please consult your healthcare provider.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_jQKcpK": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What if I don't see results in 90 days?",
            "answer": "<p>90 days is when results begin to become visible. Full results compound between 4–6 months as your follicles complete additional growth cycles. If you've been consistent and you're not seeing the results you expected, the most common reasons are: an underlying root cause that needs medical evaluation (often thyroid or ferritin), or an inconsistent daily dose.</p><p>Individual results vary based on age, genetics, health, stress, and consistency. HairScripts™ does not guarantee specific results, timelines, or outcomes. For complete details, please see our Terms & Conditions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_RdUHCz": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What happens if I stop taking HairScripts™?",
            "answer": "<p>Hair growth is an ongoing biological process. Your follicles need consistent nutritional and hormonal support to maintain results. If you stop taking HairScripts™, the underlying drivers — cortisol, DHT activity, nutrient depletion, oxidative stress — will return to their pre-supplement levels. Over time, your hair may revert.</p><p>This isn't a 30-day cleanse. It's a long-term wellness commitment. Most women who see significant results choose to stay on the formula at a maintenance level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_nXeKGy": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "What if I've had thinning for years — is it too late?",
            "answer": "<p>It's almost never too late. Follicles that have been miniaturized are still alive — they're being biochemically suppressed. As long as the follicle hasn't completely scarred over, intervention works. The key variable is consistency over time.</p><p>Women with long-standing thinning often need more time to see results — 6 months minimum, sometimes 12 months for full transformation. The follicles need extra time to reverse years of cumulative damage. But the recovery is real, and it compounds.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_GcfXKD": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "How will I know it's working?",
            "answer": "<p>The signs in order: less shedding in the shower and on your brush (weeks 4–8), scalp feels healthier and less reactive (weeks 6–12), visible baby hairs at the hairline and part (months 3–4), and noticeable density and fullness (months 4–6).</p><p>Take a photo of your part, edges, and crown the day you start — same lighting, same angle. Compare every 30 days. The day-to-day changes are too small to see in the mirror, but the month-to-month progress is undeniable when you have the photos to compare.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_X7QgJj": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_3",
            "question": "Are there any side effects?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ is formulated with clinically-studied ingredients that are generally well-tolerated. Some women report mild stomach sensitivity when taking the capsules on a completely empty stomach — if this happens, take with food. A small percentage of women may experience initial fatigue or temporary digestive changes during the first 1–2 weeks as their body adjusts to the iron and adaptogenic ingredients.</p><p>If you experience anything unusual or have concerns about an existing health condition, please discontinue use and consult your healthcare provider.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_BVCw9J": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "How does the subscription work?",
            "answer": "<p>Choose your supply (Monthly, Quarterly, or Semi-Annual), and HairScripts™ ships to your door automatically at the frequency you selected (every 30, 90, or 180 days). Your payment method on file is charged automatically on each renewal date.</p><p>By signing up for a subscription, you authorize recurring charges at the interval you chose until you cancel. You can manage everything from your customer portal at hairscriptsbybevy.com. For complete subscription terms, please see our Subscription Management policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_qyjdbz": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Can I cancel or pause my subscription anytime?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. You can cancel or pause your subscription at any time through your customer portal at hairscriptsbybevy.com, or by emailing support@hairscriptsbybevy.com.</p><p>Important: cancellations must be received before your next renewal date in order to stop the upcoming charge. Once a renewal has processed and the order has entered fulfillment, the 12-hour change window applies to that order just like any new order. For full details, please see our Subscription Management policy and our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_EEJJ9V": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Can I change my order after I place it?",
            "answer": "<p>You have a 12-hour window from the moment you place your order to cancel, change your shipping address, modify your quantity, or adjust your product selection. Email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com with your order number and the change you need.</p><p>After the 12-hour window closes, your order moves into our fulfillment queue and we can no longer make any changes to it. This is a strict cutoff with no exceptions. Once your order is picked, packed, and labeled, the address on the label is final and the order ships as-is.</p><p>Please take a moment at checkout to confirm your shipping address, your product selection, and your quantity before submitting your order. For complete details, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_NyNBNJ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What's your shipping policy?",
            "answer": "<p>HairScripts™ currently ships within the United States only. Free shipping on all subscription orders. One-time orders ship at standard rates calculated at checkout. Most orders ship within 2–5 business days from the date of order, and you'll receive a tracking number by email once your package is on its way.</p><p>Shipping times do not include weekends, federal holidays, or processing time at the fulfillment center. For complete shipping details — including address accuracy requirements and delivery acceptance — please see our Shipping & Delivery policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6XHyDH": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "Do you ship internationally?",
            "answer": "<p>Not at this time. HairScripts™ currently ships within the United States only. We're focused on serving our US customers first — and we appreciate your patience as we grow.</p><p>If you're outside the US and want to be notified when international shipping becomes available, please email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com and we'll add you to the waitlist.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_6P4V78": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What's your return and refund policy?",
            "answer": "<p>All sales are final. Because HairScripts™ is a consumable supplement product, we do not offer refunds once an order has shipped — opened or unopened.</p><p>You have a 12-hour window from the moment you place your order to cancel and receive a full refund. After 12 hours, your order enters our fulfillment queue and the sale is final. No exceptions.</p><p>The only other exceptions: (1) damaged or defective products are eligible for replacement when reported within 7 days of delivery with photo documentation, and (2) subscription renewals processed due to a verified system error on our end will be refunded or credited within 5 business days.</p><p>Hair growth takes time — most women don't see meaningful results until the 90-day mark. We encourage you to read through our science page, customer testimonials, and ingredient breakdown before purchasing. For complete details, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_TReYFQ": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What if my package is lost or stolen after delivery?",
            "answer": "<p>Once your package has been shipped and the carrier provides proof of delivery — a tracking number, timestamped photo, GPS coordinates, signature, or call attempt — HairScripts™ is no longer responsible for the package. At that point, the package has left our hands and the responsibility is between the recipient and the carrier.</p><p>If your tracking shows your package as delivered and you can't locate it: check your front door, mailroom, building lobby, and with neighbors. Wait 24–48 hours — some carriers mark packages as delivered before the actual drop-off. If you still can't find it, you'll need to file a claim directly with the shipping carrier using your tracking number. The carrier is responsible for investigating delivery disputes — not HairScripts™.</p><p>We're happy to provide the proof of delivery documentation we received from the carrier to support your claim. Email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com with your order number to request it. We do not replace bottles for packages marked as delivered. For complete details, please see our Returns & Refunds policy.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_QBbDK7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "category_4",
            "question": "What if my package arrives damaged?",
            "answer": "<p>If your bottles arrive physically damaged — broken, leaking, crushed, or otherwise unusable — we'll take care of you. Email support@hairscriptsbybevy.com within 7 days of receiving your package with your order number, clear photos of the damaged bottles, clear photos of the shipping packaging, and a short description of what happened.</p><p>Once we verify the damage, we'll reship the affected bottles to you at no additional cost and file the carrier claim on our end. Damage claims must be reported within 7 days of delivery — reports submitted after that window are not eligible for replacement, as we cannot file a successful claim with the carrier outside their reporting window.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
